# ____title____
#
# A tour of a screen. `pnpm build` says it and films the page in index.html.
# In a walkthrough a pointer goes to whatever the script is speaking of:
#
#   [slide log]           show the screen the page calls `log`
#   [slide log step:2]    send the pointer to the part marked data-step="2"
#
@characters
NARRATOR: { persona: narrator, name: ____fullName____, title: ____role____ }
---
[speakers captions]
[slide welcome]
NARRATOR: This is a tour of the harbour log. It takes half a minute.
[slide log]
NARRATOR: Every boat that comes in gets a line here.
[slide log step:1]
NARRATOR: The newest is at the top.
[slide log step:2]
NARRATOR: Search finds a boat by her name.
[slide log step:3]
NARRATOR: And this button writes a new line.
[slide entry]
NARRATOR: A new line asks for three things.
[slide entry step:1]
NARRATOR: The name of the boat.
[slide entry step:2]
NARRATOR: When she came in.
[slide entry step:3]
NARRATOR: Then save, and she is in the log.
[pause 0.4]
[slide close]
NARRATOR: That is the whole of it.
